Z||000000||paulg||10-04-1999||01:41 PM||||I'm calling around for a new engine (facotry rebuild) and someone recommended a Jasper engine. What is that? Is it any good? Is that a stock motor?||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||10-04-1999||01:58 PM||||they remanufacture engines, and many types of transmissions.....sadly, they no longer remanufacture getrag muncie 5's (:<BR><p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 10-04-1999).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||Carrolles||10-04-1999||02:50 PM||||I just picked up a Grooms remanufactured 2.8L long block from Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory in Huntsville.  It is completely stock except for being bored out .040 and comes with an 18 month unlimited mileage warranty for $1175.00.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||10-04-1999||07:36 PM||||Does it perform any better than the original engine? I was thinking about FOCOA's 3.1 conversion kit when it's time to replace mine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||10-05-1999||07:15 AM||||I looked into the FOCOA 3.1 conversion also but decided on the remanufactured long block because I don't have time to do a rebuild right now.<P>The machine work for my block was going to run around $550 to $600.  Add the $1000 for the 3.1 kit and $90 for a flywheel and it priced itself out of my current options.<P>I just picked the motor up this past weekend.  I'll start the assembly when I get home this weekend.<P>I've ported the intake and exhaust and am replacing the plug wires/dist cap/rotor.<P>I'll let you know how it feels when I get it back on the road.  It may take a while since I can only work on it on Saturdays.  I'm also converting the A/C to R134, installing JC Whitney Cruise control, Addco rear sway bar, and power windows and locks, and clutch.  I'm going to be busy for a few weekends.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88 Fiero||10-05-1999||10:45 AM||||For the same amount of money why not just get a '94 - '95 3.4 camaro block...the engine is a good swap to the 2.8 block.. it looks stock, has more ribbed for durability..a compression of 9.1 and has a torque of 200 lbs...turbo charge it or nitrous it...you'll get better results with it...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||10-05-1999||07:22 PM||||Are there any kits involved in this Camaro 3.4 swap or does it fit to a tee?<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 10-05-1999).]||||reg||5
Z||000007||Eddie||10-05-1999||08:28 PM||||Hay Paulg<BR>Ichecked into TO THE GRAY COLORED MOTORS (Jasper)they are very nice will done motors. but if your thinking you wuold like some more power Jasper will not do it stock only!! I had guy at a machine shop do mine from the oil pan to the valve cover for what jasper charges I had my motor done the way I wanted it!!||||reg||4
Z||000008||Cooter||10-05-1999||11:21 PM||||A while back, we bought a 350 Chevy from Jasper for an 88 pickup. It was a very good and smooth running engine and has run over 100,000 miles since being installed. Unfortunatly, it was too expensive for a stock motor. ||||reg||14
Z||000009||Carrolles||10-06-1999||07:21 AM||||The Camare/Firebird 3.4L engine is an excelent choice for the Fiero but it does require some modifications to make it fit.  The starter must be moved to the opposite side which requires drilling a hole in an angled boss (requires a jig to do).  Also it will require a late model Fiero flywheel or the 3.4L flywheel.  You will also need to weld a stud onto the A/C bracket to mount the shock strut.  Use the 3/4L injectors or get an adjustable fuel pressure regulator.<P>I considered going this route but don't have the time to do the work myself right now.||||reg||1
Z||000010||sluppy123||10-06-1999||09:31 PM||||I just finished installing a Jasper longblock in my 87' GT. For $950 I got a internaly stock engine with a high volume sealed power oil pump plus a 3-year 36,000 mile warranty. I think it was a fairly good deal, this was my first time doing any kind of engine swap so I went the easy way.||||reg||14
Z||000011||Eddie||10-07-1999||05:19 PM||||Sluppy123 <BR>	GREAT DEAL FOR $900 . In NJ THEY RUN ABOUT  $1500.00 INSTALLED FOR $24 ,$2500.00 jasper motors are realy nice .||||reg||5
